## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design multi-source ingestion pipelines with basic deduplication and schema handling for an entry-level data engineering position.

## Key Concepts
- Change data capture (CDC) from MongoDB
- Batch ingestion from SFTP
- Canonical schema design vs. source schema
- Idempotent writes and deduplication strategies
- Lightweight testing for data contracts and schema drift

## Code Example
```javascript
function enforceContract(rec) {
  const required = ['customer_id', 'event_ts', 'value'];
  const missing = required.filter(field => rec[field] == null);
  if (missing.length > 0) {
    throw new Error(`Missing required fields: ${missing.join(', ')}`);
  }
  if (typeof rec.value !== 'number') {
    throw new Error('Value must be numeric');
  }
  return rec;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical, beginner-friendly construction of a data pipeline with common tasks: deduplication, validation, timestamp handling, and partitioned Parquet, plus testing and monitoring.

## Key Concepts
- JSON Lines parsing
- Idempotent deduplication
- Data quality checks (required fields, types)
- Timestamp normalization to UTC
- Parquet writing and date partitioning
- Basic testing and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const readline = require('readline');
(async () => {
  const rl = readline.createInterface({ input: fs.createReadStream('logs.jsonl'), crlfDelay: Infinity });
  const seen = new Set();
  for await (const line of rl) {
    const obj = JSON.parse(line);
    if (!obj.user_id || !obj.timestamp || !obj.path || !obj.status) continue;
    const key = `${obj.timestamp}|${obj.user_id}|${obj.path}`;
    if (seen.has(key)) continue;
    seen.add(key);
    // normalization and persistence would occur here
  }
})();
```

